AWS Storage Face-off: S3 vs EBS

When working on the cloud, one of the most common questions is – Where should I store my data?
On AWS, two popular choices come up: Amazon S3 and Amazon EBS.

🔹 Amazon S3 (Simple Storage Service)

Object storage (best for files, backups, images, media)

Virtually unlimited storage capacity

11 9’s durability (99.999999999%)

Data accessible from anywhere via HTTP/HTTPS

Use cases → Backups, Big Data, Static Websites, Media Hosting


🔹 Amazon EBS (Elastic Block Store)

Block storage (acts like a hard disk for EC2 instances)

Low-latency, consistent performance

Fixed size allocation (e.g., 100GB, 500GB)

Tied to a specific AZ/Region with EC2

Use cases → Databases, Operating Systems, Application storage


⚡ Simple Rule of Thumb:

Need scalable, cost-effective, globally accessible storage → Go with S3 ✅

Need fast, disk-like storage for EC2 → Go with EBS ✅


💡 Pro Tip: Use them together → Run your app on EC2 + EBS while storing backups/logs on S3.
